      <statement><p>A child inflates a balloon, admires it for a while and then lets the
air out.  If <m>V(t)</m> gives the volume  of the
balloon at time <m>t</m>, then the figure below shows  <m>V'(t)</m> as a
function of <m>t</m>.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/webwork-26-image-1.png" width="66%"/>
<p>At what time does the child:</p>
<p><alert>A.</alert>
Begin to inflate the balloon?
<m>t =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert>B.</alert>
Finish inflating the balloon?
<m>t =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert>C.</alert>
Begin to let the air out?
<m>t =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><em>(What would the graph of <m>V'(t)</m> look like if the child had alternated between pinching and releasing the open end of the balloon, instead of letting the air out at constant rate?)</em></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>3</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>9</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>14</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <solution><m>V'(t)</m> becomes positive,
